# Technical SEO

Every routable page must use `<Seo />` from `@/components/Seo` with unique `title`, `description`, and correct `path`.

## Titles & meta

- Title: primary keyword + benefit; brand appended by `Seo` (`| RidgeRise Media`) unless already present
- Keep titles ≤ ~60 chars before brand suffix; descriptions 140–160 chars, one clear promise, no stuffing
- Match page-owned search concept (see seo-strategy): home = performance customer acquisition; specialty pages own their layer — not all “Pay Per Call”
- Buyer/home meta emphasize customer acquisition + in-house media buying; avoid commodity “buy calls/leads” language
- Pass `keywords` only when they mirror real on-page terms (verticals, blog tags) — never invent long keyword lists
- Use `type="article"` + `publishedTime` / `modifiedTime` on blog posts
- Prefer `/assets/og-default.jpg` or a page-specific OG image (≥1200×630); always set meaningful `image` alt via title

## Canonical & URLs

- `path` must match the live route (`/`, `/publishers`, `/verticals/auto-insurance`, etc.)
- Site origin is `site.url` (`https://ridgerisemedia.com`) — no trailing slash except home
- Never invent alternate domains or duplicate paths for the same content

## Structured data

- Default Organization + WebSite JSON-LD comes from `Seo` — do not duplicate on every page
- Add page-specific `jsonLd` when useful: FAQPage, BreadcrumbList, Service, Article extras
- Valid schema.org types only; keep strings consistent with visible copy

## On-page structure

- Exactly one `<h1>` per page; nest `h2` → `h3` without skipping levels
- Descriptive internal links (avoid “click here”); link publishers ↔ buyers ↔ verticals ↔ blog where relevant
- Images: descriptive `alt`; decorative images use empty `alt=""`
- FAQ sections: question as heading or accessible label; answers in plain text for FAQ schema alignment

## Do not

```tsx
// ❌ Missing Seo, generic title, wrong path
<Seo title="Home" description="Welcome" path="/home" />

// ✅ Unique, page-owned concept, route-accurate
<Seo
  title="Customer Acquisition for Advertisers"
  description="RidgeRise Media builds performance marketing campaigns that turn digital demand into qualified inbound calls through in-house media buying and Pay Per Call."
  path="/buyers"
  keywords={["customer acquisition", "performance marketing", "inbound calls"]}
/>
```
